  "ablation_size_label": "size = 268,435,456 (2.15 GB total traffic)",
  "takeaways": [
    "**Warp-Uniform Collective Synchronization:** Modern CUDA architectures enforce strict warp-synchrony on shuffle-up (shfl.sync.up with full mask 0xFFFFFFFF). Branching before calling warp-scan deadlocks the warp; the idiomatic Crisp solution is having all 32 lanes uniformly participate in the warp collective with neutral values (0.0).",
    "**Memory Coalescing Dominance:** Comparing 4 elements/thread against 8 elements/thread on H100 revealed a 2.2x slowdown (2.16 ms vs 4.83 ms) when widening thread stride across warps, proving that maintaining 128-byte aligned coalesced memory transactions is the primary determinant of scan performance on HBM3/HBM3e.",
    "**High-Throughput Declarative Scan:** Crisp 2-pass hierarchical prefix sum achieved over 4.16 TB/s DRAM traffic on B200 (1.03 ms) and 1.99 TB/s on H100 (2.16 ms) in just 35 SLOC of clean, idiomatic Crisp without manual pointer chasing or PTX inline hacks."
  ],
